audio.cpp fork delta: explicit ggml lowering APIs, ported 2026-09-23 for the
audio.cpp merge up to 9bdd1d90 (v0.8.2). Source commit: audio.cpp #532
(07490d83, "Add explicit ggml lowering APIs"). Upstream engine code calls this
surface from engine_core (wan_video_vae_runtime, linear / primitive /
structural modules), so nothing builds without it.

  - New lowering enums and setters: ggml_mul_mat_set_lowering (op_params slot
    1, values 0/2/3 - 1 is taken by ggml_mul_mat_set_hint's
    GGML_HINT_SRC0_IS_HADAMARD in the same slot), ggml_concat_set_lowering,
    ggml_im2col_2d_set_lowering (slot 7), ggml_im2col_3d_set_lowering (slot
    10), ggml_rms_norm_channels_set_lowering,
    ggml_conv_3d_concat_pad_spatial_gemm_set_lowering.
  - New ops appended after GGML_OP_IM2COL_ASYM: CONV_3D_CONCAT_PAD_SPATIAL_GEMM,
    RMS_NORM_CHANNELS{,_SILU,_ADD_BIAS_SILU}, ROPE_INTERLEAVED_PAIRS, with
    builders (ggml_rope_interleaved_pairs, ggml_rms_norm_channels*,
    ggml_conv_3d_concat_pad_spatial_gemm{,_ex}). GGML_OP_COUNT 109 -> 114.
  - ggml_add_cast_impl accepts full broadcast (ggml_can_repeat) instead of row
    repeat. Safe on CPU: an F16/BF16 src0 takes the modulo-broadcasting binary
    kernel, and the only caller (wan_video_vae_runtime) passes an un-repeated
    bias only on its CUDA fast path.

Port notes: 3-way merged onto 0.24.0 with LF-normalized sides (audio.cpp stores
these files CRLF). Conflicts: the op-count asserts, and ggml_graph_set_n_nodes
(ours) beside ggml_mul_mat_set_lowering (theirs) - both kept.

NOT PORTED YET (tracked in MULTI_AGENT_FUSION_PLAN_AND_TRACKER.md): the CUDA
implementations of these lowerings and ops (audio.cpp 62c664af, 1709+/548-
lines over 12 ggml-cuda files, conflicting with 0.24.0 in concat.cu,
quantize.cu[h], mmq.cu and ggml-cuda.cu). Until then the lowerings are ignored
(they are hints) and the five new ops are unsupported on every backend - 0015
makes the CPU say so. Only LiveAvatar / Wan S2V use them.

